## API Endpoints

### Risks (cyberrx-api/src/routes/risks.js)
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| POST | /api/risks | Create risk with correlation linkage |
| GET | /api/risks | List risks (filterable by severity, status, businessProcessId) |
| GET | /api/risks/high-exposure | Get risks with high financial exposure |
| GET | /api/risks/by-business-process/:id | Get risks for a business process |
| GET | /api/risks/by-asset/:id | Get risks for an asset |
| GET | /api/risks/:id | Get specific risk |
| PUT | /api/risks/:id | Update risk |
| DELETE | /api/risks/:id | Delete risk |

### Findings (cyberrx-api/src/routes/findings.js)
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| POST | /api/findings | Create finding with auto repeat detection |
| GET | /api/findings | List findings (filterable by severity, status, asset, etc.) |
| GET | /api/findings/statistics | Get finding statistics |
| GET | /api/findings/repeats | Get repeat findings |
| GET | /api/findings/by-risk/:id | Get findings for a risk |
| GET | /api/findings/by-asset/:id | Get findings for an asset |
| GET | /api/findings/:id | Get specific finding |
| PUT | /api/findings/:id | Update finding |
| POST | /api/findings/:id/mark-repeat | Manually mark as repeat |
| DELETE | /api/findings/:id | Delete finding |

---

## Correlation Linkage Implemented

### Risk Entity Fields
- **businessProcessIds**: JSONB array linking to business processes
- **dataObjectIds**: JSONB array linking to data objects (PHI/PII/PCI)
- **threatScenarioId**: Link to threat scenario (ransomware, phishing, etc.)
- **frameworkMappings**: JSONB array for NIST, HIPAA, CIS references
- **financialExposure**: Numeric financial impact
- **costToRemediate**: Numeric remediation cost
- **legalObligationIds**: JSONB array linking to legal obligations
- **regulatoryCitation**: Free-text regulatory citation
- **executiveOwner**: Executive role/user responsible
- **remediationOwner**: Remediation owner
- **evidenceOwner**: Evidence owner
- **auditEvidenceRequired**: Audit evidence requirements text
- **auditTestIds**: JSONB array linking to audit tests

### Finding Entity Fields
- **riskId**: Link to risk record
- **assetId**: Link to affected asset
- **applicationId**: Link to affected application
- **businessProcessId**: Link to affected business process
- **isRepeat**: Boolean for repeat detection
- **originalFindingId**: Original finding when repeat
- **repeatCount**: Count of repeats
- **remediationPlan**: Remediation plan text
- **targetDate**: Target resolution date
- **owner**: Finding owner
- **source**: Finding source (scanner, manual)
- **sourceRef**: Source reference ID
- **tool**: Tool that generated finding
- **metadata**: Additional metadata JSONB

---

## Repeat Detection

The Finding model includes automatic repeat detection:
1. On finding creation, checks for similar existing findings
2. Similarity based on title, asset, and tool
3. Auto-marks as repeat with incremented count if match found
4. Manual endpoint to mark as repeat

---

## Acceptance Criteria

- [x] Risk carries businessProcessId[], dataObjectIds[], threatScenarioId
- [x] Risk carries frameworkMappings[], financialExposure, legalObligationId[]
- [x] Risk carries executiveOwner, remediationOwner, evidenceOwner
- [x] Risk carries auditEvidenceRequired, auditTestIds[]
- [x] Finding links to riskId, assetId, businessProcessId
- [x] Finding supports repeat detection fields (isRepeat, originalFindingId, repeatCount)
- [x] Migrations run cleanly and preserve existing data
- [x] All entities properly reference orgs(id) with ON DELETE CASCADE
- [x] GIN indexes on JSONB arrays for efficient queries
- [x] All endpoints are JWT-authenticated and org-scoped

